! Silicon, 2 atoms in the primitive fcc cell, PAW, PBE.
!
! si2-paw.in under PBE, and the case that exercises the one-centre gradient
! machinery: a radial derivative on each atom's own mesh, an angular gradient
! taken from the harmonics' derivatives, and a spherical divergence, on a
! quadrature that has grown from 28 directions to 45 because the functional is
! gradient-corrected. QE prints the one-centre energy as its own term, so that
! machinery is checked directly and not only through the total.
!
! conv_thr is tightened far past what the answer needs so that both codes run to
! the same fixed point and the energy terms can be compared digit by digit.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav=2, celldm(1)=10.20, nat=2, ntyp=1,
    ecutwfc=20.0, ecutrho=160.0
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si  28.086  Si.pbe-n-kjpaw_psl.0.1.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Si 0.00 0.00 0.00
 Si 0.25 0.25 0.25
K_POINTS
  2
   0.250000  0.250000  0.250000   1.00
   0.250000  0.250000  0.750000   3.00
